Add dtiMerge, a CLI for merging checkpoints and LoRAs

Upstream mixes models in the macOS app only.  What survives in the open
tree is Libraries/DataModels/Sources/mixing.fbs, the recipe schema, with
no consumer, so the mode names and the 0.6 LoRA default follow it.

LoRALoader.mergeLoRA supplies the LoRA arithmetic unchanged.  It is a
function of name, dataType and shape, so driving it from a store's own
key list needs no built model graph, and LoRAImporter has already folded
alpha over rank into the stored factors, which leaves strength a plain
scalar.

Quantized and ezm7 inputs promote to raw, both being lossy.  Datatypes
are preserved per tensor because ccv_nnc_tensor_read cannot convert 16F
to 16BF and LTX-2.3 carries four 16BF tensors inside an otherwise f16
conversion.  Shapes reconcile squeezed, since a q6p conversion writes
[1, 1, 1, 128] where the f16 one writes [128].
